[SIZE=6][B][COLOR=#00AF5C]Gameplay[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]

Players drop into cages at the start of each round. After the countdown, cages open and everyone scrambles to build a pillar and fight for survival. The last team (or player) alive wins.

[SIZE=4][B]Multi-Instance Arenas[/B][/SIZE]
Run multiple simultaneous games on the same server, each in its own isolated world. Set a number in [ICODE]config.yml[/ICODE] and LocoPillars handles the rest.

[SIZE=4][B]Team Support[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*]Configurable players-per-team and number of teams
[*]Team-colored leather armor
[*]Team chat ([ICODE]/teamchat[/ICODE])
[*]Team status on scoreboard & TAB list
[/LIST]


[SIZE=6][B][COLOR=#00AF5C]LuckyBlocks[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]

LuckyBlocks are fully scriptable. Each block is its own folder containing a [ICODE]Settings.json[/ICODE] for metadata and a [ICODE]Luckyblock.kts[/ICODE] for the effect. The plugin ships with [B]50 pre-designed LuckyBlocks[/B]. Drop a new folder into [ICODE]plugins/LocoPillars/Luckyblocks/[/ICODE] and it gets picked up automatically with no restart needed.

[SIZE=4][B]Settings.json[/B][/SIZE]
[CODE=json]{
  "id": "firework_frenzy",
  "display_name": "Firework Frenzy",
  "description": "Colorful fireworks explode in every direction!",
  "icon": {
    "material": "FIREWORK_ROCKET",
    "custom_model_data": 0
  },
  "block_type": "LUCKY_BLOCK",
  "rarity": "COMMON"
}[/CODE]

Rarity options: [ICODE]COMMON[/ICODE] [ICODE]UNCOMMON[/ICODE] [ICODE]RARE[/ICODE] [ICODE]EPIC[/ICODE] [ICODE]LEGENDARY[/ICODE]. Chances per rarity are configured in [ICODE]config.yml[/ICODE].

[SIZE=4][B]Luckyblock.kts[/B][/SIZE]

The script receives [ICODE]player[/ICODE] (who broke the block) and [ICODE]game[/ICODE] (utility helper). The full Bukkit/Paper API is available.

[CODE=kotlin]repeat(5) {
    val offset = player.location.clone().add(
        Math.random() * 4 - 2, 0.0, Math.random() * 4 - 2
    )
    game.spawnFirework(offset)
}
game.playSound(player, org.bukkit.Sound.ENTITY_FIREWORK_ROCKET_LAUNCH, 1.0f, 1.0f)
game.sendTitle(player, "§6Firework Frenzy!", "§7Celebrate!", 5, 50, 10)[/CODE]


[SIZE=6][B][COLOR=#00AF5C]Cosmetics[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]

Cosmetics work the same way as LuckyBlocks. Each cosmetic is a folder under [ICODE]plugins/LocoPillars/Cosmetics/<type>/[/ICODE] with a [ICODE]Settings.json[/ICODE] and a [ICODE]Cosmetic.kts[/ICODE] script. The plugin ships with [B]64 pre-designed cosmetics[/B] across four categories. Players buy and equip cosmetics through [ICODE]/cosmetics[/ICODE] using in-game coins.

[TABLE]
[TR]
[TH]Type[/TH]
[TH]Count[/TH]
[TH]Trigger[/TH]
[/TR]
[TR]
[TD]Kill effects[/TD]
[TD]20[/TD]
[TD]Triggered when the player gets a kill[/TD]
[/TR]
[TR]
[TD]Death effects[/TD]
[TD]20[/TD]
[TD]Triggered when the player is eliminated[/TD]
[/TR]
[TR]
[TD]Win effects[/TD]
[TD]20[/TD]
[TD]Triggered when the player's team wins[/TD]
[/TR]
[TR]
[TD]Cages[/TD]
[TD]4[/TD]
[TD]The skin used for the spawn cage[/TD]
[/TR]
[/TABLE]

[SIZE=4][B]Settings.json[/B][/SIZE]
[CODE=json]{
  "id": "firework_kill",
  "type": "KILL",
  "display_name": "§6Firework Kill",
  "lore": ["§7Launch a firework on every kill!"],
  "price": 300,
  "required_level": 3,
  "permission": "",
  "rarity": "UNCOMMON",
  "active": true,
  "icon": {
    "material": "FIREWORK_ROCKET",
    "custom_model_data": 0
  }
}[/CODE]

[SIZE=4][B]Cosmetic.kts[/B][/SIZE]

The script receives [ICODE]player[/ICODE] (the cosmetic owner, killer for kill effects or the eliminated player for death effects) and [ICODE]game[/ICODE].

[CODE=kotlin]game.spawnFirework(player.location.add(0.0, 0.5, 0.0))
game.spawnParticles(player.location.add(0.0, 1.0, 0.0), org.bukkit.Particle.FIREWORK, 20, 0.5, 0.5, 0.5, 0.1)[/CODE]


[SIZE=6][B][COLOR=#00AF5C]Voting Events[/COLOR] [COLOR=#888888](Coming Soon)[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]

Voting events are mid-game modifiers that players vote on during a game. This system uses the same module-based approach as LuckyBlocks and Cosmetics. Drop a folder into [ICODE]plugins/LocoPillars/modules/voting/[/ICODE] and it becomes available in-game without a restart.

[SIZE=4][B]settings.json[/B][/SIZE]
[CODE=json]{
  "id": "no_fall_mode",
  "display_name": "No Fall Mode",
  "description": "Fall damage is completely disabled for everyone in this round.",
  "icon": {
    "material": "FEATHER",
    "custom_model_data": 0
  },
  "active": true,
  "vote_weight": 1,
  "duration": -1,
  "announce": {
    "title": "§6§lNo Fall Mode!",
    "subtitle": "§7Fall damage is disabled!",
    "chat": "§6[Event] §eNo Fall Mode is now active!"
  }
}[/CODE]

[SIZE=4][B]script.kts[/B][/SIZE]

The script receives [ICODE]game[/ICODE] and [ICODE]players[/ICODE]. Use [ICODE]game.registerEventListener[/ICODE] to hook into Bukkit events. The listener is automatically cleaned up when the game ends.

[CODE=kotlin]game.sendTitle("§6§lNo Fall Mode!", "§7Fall damage is disabled!", 10, 60, 10)
game.broadcast("§6[Event] §eNo Fall Mode is now active!")

game.getPlayers().forEach { player ->
    player.playSound(player.location, org.bukkit.Sound.ENTITY_PLAYER_LEVELUP, 1.0f, 1.2f)
}

game.registerEventListener<org.bukkit.event.entity.EntityDamageEvent> { event ->
    val entity = event.entity
    if (entity is org.bukkit.entity.Player &&
        game.isPlayerInGame(entity) &&
        event.cause == org.bukkit.event.entity.EntityDamageEvent.DamageCause.FALL
    ) {
        event.isCancelled = true
    }
}[/CODE]


[SIZE=6][B][COLOR=#00AF5C]Achievements[/COLOR][/B][/SIZE]

27+ built-in achievements across 4 difficulty tiers, each with configurable XP and coin rewards. Add your own by dropping a [ICODE].yml[/ICODE] file in [ICODE]plugins/LocoPillars/Achievements/[/ICODE].

